== 4. New probes for round 5: probe-r5.sh (Run) ==
T1, T2: a role's move cut short. The new id is marked at its next hook and refused; the
role stays free, also after the operator gave it elsewhere and it fell free; handoff role
gives it back. In T1, before that next hook, the new id has no file, and its note with
--as is posted (my note 1). T3: a mark's move cut short leaves both ids marked.
W, X: chains with a resumed old id, and with the role given again at each step.
V: a hook with a fixed role carries an unmarked role; a session with no history gets the
fixed role and no file.

