== 5. Reviewer-2's #422: probe-r5y.sh (Run) ==
It reproduces. With a hook that fixes the role, while the marked old process still runs
past the wait (cut here to 300 ms; 5 s in use), the new id listens as reviewer, takes a
note, and its own note is posted. Once the old process ends, its next hook carries the
mark and it is refused. A new session with no history listens as reviewer by the same
hook. (The second note in the probe was refused as identical to the first; the line
that matters there is N's "nothing new for reviewer".)

